\details{
v1 walk-forward scores scalar train-window candidates, selects one candidate
per fold, and runs only that selected candidate on the matching test window.
It is not PBO, CSCV, CPCV, DSR, benchmark-relative diagnostics, OMS,
paper/live trading, or a selection-integrity correction. Walk-forward
evidence is only as survivorship-safe as the sealed snapshot and universe
semantics it evaluates.

With the default \code{opening_state_policy = "carry_test_state"}, test windows
are path-dependent: each completed selected test run can seed the next test
opening state. Per-fold test metrics are therefore not independent. Carrying
needs test windows in time order that touch exactly: when a trading day lies
between two consecutive test windows, positions would cross it unvalued, and
when a test window starts before the previous one ends (overlap or reverse
order), it would open from that window's later state. The call refuses both
before running anything, with \code{ledgr_walk_forward_gapped_carry} or
\code{ledgr_walk_forward_overlapping_carry}. Use folds whose \code{step} equals
\code{test_window}, or \code{"flat_test_state"}, which accepts any layout.

Rerunning a session with the same arguments reuses its finished test runs
as recorded and resumes a test run that an interruption left unfinished.
Fold boundaries on the snapshot's first or last date resolve to its first
or last session; a date outside the snapshot refuses. Anchored
fold definitions intentionally grow the train window over time, so compute
cost grows with later folds and larger candidate grids. \code{metric_diff_abs} is
\code{test_metric_value - train_metric_value}; whether a positive value indicates
improvement or degradation depends on the selection rule direction.

In an availability-aware session every training and test window reads
feature, mark and entitlement history from the data start (the first
session of the snapshot) through one shared causal preparation; windows only
bound decisions. Under \code{"carry_test_state"} the test windows form one
economic chain: each window except the last executes its final decision at
the following session's open, and the next window opens from the resulting
cash, positions, FIFO lots, unsettled corporate-action entitlements and
frozen holdings. Strategy state does not cross a window. The chain equals one
run with the selected parameters switching at the same decision pulses.
The last window, \code{"flat_test_state"} windows and standalone runs keep the
terminal rule: a final decision is recorded but not executed. Dense sessions
keep their per-window feature start. This is separate from
\code{cold_start_distorted}, which concerns opening positions, not features.
}
